\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Apr dlr sales estimated at $21.35 bln-bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 1 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) sold an estimated $21.35 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in April, bankers said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  BOJ data showed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) received 2.7752 trillion yen from the private sector in April through its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say MOF's receipts from the private sector less its sales of financing bills (FBs) roughly represent the amount of dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in yen terms. \par \par \uc2  MOF's FB sales to the private sector were zero in April. \par \par \uc2  The private sector comprises commercial banks, foreign central banks, municipal governments, public funds and quasi-governmental institutions. \par \par \uc2  MOF has confirmed that the BOJ stepped into the market to sell dollars on April 9 in New York. Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was detected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily on the following day in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The dollar moved in a range of 127.40 yen to 133.50 yen on those days in New York and Tokyo trade. \par \par \uc2  Some bankers said the BOJ may have also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  quietly on other days in April. \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo trade during the month, the dollar hit a high of 135.20 yen on April 3 and April 6, and a low of 127.40 yen on April 10. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limite