\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar/yen forges ahead by midday Europe. \b0\par\par\uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 1 (Reuters) - The dollar set three-week highs against the yen while the mark was at 14-1/2 month highs against the yen by midday Europe, as concern over Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  waned, traders and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gone away," said a trader from a U.S. bank. "Look how much the Bank of Japan sold in April, and the market is still up here." \par \par \uc2  Bankers said on Friday the Bank of Japan spent a record $21.35 bln selling dollars for yen in April. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was trading at 133.35/40 at 1001 GMT, up over a yen from 132.15/20 in late Europe on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was at its highest level since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry confirmed BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on April 9. \par \par \uc2  Mark/yen rose to its highest in 14-1/2 months, and was just off 74.41 highs at 74.33/37, from 73.63/65 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said dollar/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk had not faded entirely, helping mark/yen gains in favour of the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The yen was also weakened by Japanese March household spending, which fell 5.7 percent from a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  In addition, policy chief of the ruling LDP Taku Yamasaki told reporters in Washington Japan was considering tax system changes from a medium-to long-term perspective. \par \par \uc2  One Tokyo-based dealers said such slow debate on the tax system could not help the economy. \par \par \uc2  But activity was likely to be thin, dealers said, ahead of public holidays in Japan next week. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs, visits London for meetings with British economists and market participants on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "It will be the same old rhetoric," said Stewart Newnham, international economist at First Chicago. \par \par \uc2  "I would bet he is going to use the words 'excessive' and 'volatility'," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark was steady to softer, with most European markets closed for a public holiday on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark traded at 1.7917/22, from 1.7931/36 in late Europe on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The mark remained buoyant against the Swiss franc, as political and European Commission leaders tried to play down the row over the presidency of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) which is overshadowing this weekend's EU summit to decide 1999 single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  entrants. \par \par \uc2  European Commission president Jacques Santer said a split in the eight-year term would be damaging for the ECB. \par \par \uc2  A spokesman for British Prime Minister Tony Blair said on Friday there had been some progress on resolving the issue. The competing candidates are the Dutch Wim Duisenberg and French Jean-Claude Trichet. \par \par \uc2  Mark/Swiss was at 83.62/65, against a 6-1/2 month high of 83.66 and from 83.56/66 in late Europe on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Santer and EC Commissioner Yves-Thibault de Silguy are holding a news conference in advance of the meeting of European economic and finance ministers (ECOFIN) later on Friday to recommend EMU members. \par \par \uc2  Sterling softened following a stream of UK data. \par \par \uc2  The April manufacturing PMI index showed a contraction for the first time in nearly two years, at 49.5. \par \par \uc2  UK net consumer credit grew by a record net seasonally-adjusted 1.429 bln stg in March, and March final M4 money supply rose a seasonally-adjusted 9.8 percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  Sterling/mark eased to 2.9933/38 from 2.9989/99 in late Europe on Thursday. Cable fell to $1.6700/05 from $1.6725/35. ((Carolyn Cohn, London newsroom +44 171 542 6320, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5106315\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
