\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr eases in early Tokyo, but supported at Y132. \b0\par\par\uc2 488 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, April 30 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0014 GMT --*Dollar eased slightly against yen in early \par \par \uc2  trade after it failed to break through resistance of 132.50 yen \par \par \uc2  despite several attempts, traders said. \par \par \uc2      *Talk of options-related sales and hedge sales by trust \par \par \uc2  banks deterring dollar from rising above that level, although \par \par \uc2  stop-loss buying expected once that point broken. \par \par \uc2      *Still, sharp rise unlikely amid persistent caution over \par \par \uc2  possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      *"No one is willing to buy dollars above 132.50 yen," said \par \par \uc2  a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  *Downside well-supported by expectations of month-end commercial dollar buying at 0100 GMT and possible dollar buying relating to setting up of fresh investment trust funds. \par \par \uc2  *"Sporadic buying orders (relating to investment trust funds) were detected, which could support the dollar," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  *Commercial operators such as exporters mostly sidelined amid Golden Week Holidays here, although some selling orders seen in place above 133 yen, said a Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  *Japanese exporters also interested in selling marks for yen above 74.00 yen. Mark was at 73.60/63 yen at 0300 GMT. \par \par \uc2  *Rise of Tokyo stock market in early trade following gains in Wall Street on Wednesday had little impact on dollar/yen rate so far, said the trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  *Nikkei-225 stock index was up 174.60 points at 15,570.03 at 0034 GMT. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar eased against mark in subdued morning trade on light position adjustments ahead of weekend EU summit. \par \par \uc2  *Talk of heavy dollar sales by U.S. funds above 1.800 marks overnight and lingering concerns about U.S. assets markets likely to keep dollar soft against mark for while, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  2311 GMT \par \par \uc2  *Dollar barely moved against yen in early Asian trade on Thursday amid lack of fresh factors, with activity slow amidst Japan's Golden Week holiday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  *Options-related sales near 133 yen and caution over Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could check dollar's rise, while downside seen supported at around 131.70/80 yen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar/mark slipped on Wednesday in New York amid market caution before weekend's European Union summit and as Germany's top central banker fanned talk of a possible rate hike. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar/mark hit 1.7925 session low overnight after comments from Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer were first interpreted to mean Germany could raise rates. \par \par \uc2  *Traders said dollar climbed back from intra-session lows after Bundesbank council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher was quoted in Germany's Berliner Zeitung newspaper as saying he saw no sensible reason to raise rates in 1998. \par \par \uc2  *U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin on Tuesday said fundamental economic policy not \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was cure for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic problems and weak yen. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-1396 email:tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4u06aur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
