\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/mark down in U.S. as investors eye EU summit. \b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, April 29 (Reuters) - Dollar/mark slipped on Wednesday amid market caution before the weekend's European Union summit and as Germany's top central banker fanned talk of a possible rate hike, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, dollar/yen was little changed but firm as speculation eased over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark hit the 1.7925 session low after comments from Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer were first interpreted to mean Germany could raise rates. Speaking in Leipzig, Tietmeyer said the central monetary union rate would depend on a mix of national policies. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended lower at 1.7960/63 marks, down from 1.8022/27 at the open and at 132.25/30 yen from 132.35/45. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the U.S. unit climbed back from intrasession lows after Bundesbank council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher was quoted in Germany's Berliner Zeitung newspaper as saying he saw no sensible reason to raise rates in 1998. \par \par \uc2  "Tietmeyer started talking about looking at the global perspective of EMU and people misconstrued that as saying Germany's going to have to raise up to the central parity interest rate rather than the others coming down," said John Gariano, vice president at Sumitomo Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  "They're coming from an anemic growth pattern and they cannot afford to raise rates at this time," he added. \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank President also accused the European Commission of not outlining all facts in its convergence report that recommended 11 countries as fit to join monetary union. In particular, he noted that the Bundesbank and Economic Monetary Institute stressed that two member countries needed further debt reduction measures. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said traders were squaring positions ahead of the European Union summit this weekend when leaders will finalize monetary union membership and central parity rates. \par \par \uc2  Apart from isolated flurries of activity, flows were relatively thin and the dollar remained rangebound, trading between 1.7850-1.8050 marks and 131.50-132.50 yen, said Chris Melendez, senior dealer at Sanwa Bank California. \par \par \uc2  The dollar drifted lower as investors squared positions as Japan began celebrating the Golden Week holidays and before U.S. employment cost and growth data are released on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  However, traders said the dollar/yen was underpinned after U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin on Tuesday said fundamental economic policy not \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the cure for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic problems and the weak yen. \par \par \uc2  Koji Omi, Japan's Economic Planning Agency minister, said that Japan's economic situation had become increasingly severe in recent months, but also said the government's latest set of fiscal stimulus measures would have considerable impact. \par \par \uc2  Traders stressed that the market needs to see improvements in economic data as real proof of an economic upturn. Until then, forecasts for a weaker yen were still widespread. \par \par \uc2  "They've spent $15 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and they've knocked it down a yen and it's looking like it's ready to blow off again on the upside. Economic fundamentals keep pointing to lower interest rates," Gariano said. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the dollar was lower at 1.4977/87 Swiss francs from 1.4990/00 at the open and the British pound rose to $1.6695/05 from $1.6680/90. The dollar edged lower to Canadian $1.4362/67 from C$1.4370/75 and the Australian dollar gained to $0.6489/94 from $0.6474/79. \par \par \uc2  ((-Al Yoon, N.A. \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Unit, 212-859-1672)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4t06fff\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
