\par\par \b \uc2  Key to aiding yen is policy, not  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -Rubin. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Albert Yoon \par \uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 1998\par 05:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, April 28 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin on Tuesday welcomed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest economic package and said economic policy - not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets - was the key to bolstering the weak yen. \par \par \uc2  Rubin's statement, in response to questions after a speech to the Foreign Policy Association, buoyed the dollar in Asian trading, helping the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  overcome strong resistance at 132.30 yen. \par \par \uc2  Asked about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the ailing yen, Rubin said, "The real solution to problems with the yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  lies in fundamental economic policy, not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  He reiterated that it was important \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  act now to implement its new reform package. \par \par \uc2  "Japan has announced a substantial program and that's a positive step ... now they have to implement the program, plus they have to deal with issues of the financial sector and deregulation of markets," Rubin said. \par \par \uc2  "There's a lot to be done in Japan, but they've made a positive, substantial step," he said. \par \par \uc2  Rubin's remarks followed a similar statement by Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers in San Francisco earlier. \par \par \uc2  "Successful Japanese efforts at economic stimulus, financial restructuring and deregulation and market opening are important for Japan, Asia and the global economy," Summers told a technology conference. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also derived strength from Rubin's upbeat assessment that the greenback could successfully co-exist with Europe's planned single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro, even if the new pan-European unit was increasingly used as a reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "As long as people have confidence in our basic policy thrust and they have confidence in the economy, then I think the dollar will perform its functions in ways that are advantageous to us and I think we can co-exist with another growing reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  very well," Rubin said. \par \par \uc2  He added that if the formation of a single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  benefits Europe, that in turn would aid the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  "If it turns out it's good for Europe, then it's basically good for us," Rubin said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had edged higher against the Japanese yen in U.S. trading on Tuesday following signs the Japanese economy continued to worsen in March. \par \par \uc2  At the close of trading in New York, the dollar was little changed at 1.7948/58 marks, up from 1.7935/40 at the open. It rose to 132.18/28 yen versus 131.92/97. \par \par \uc2  Traders said dollar/mark was largely inactive ahead of this weekend's European Union summit meeting which will set the charter members of the planned monetary union. Stability of European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar was seen as the key for the successful launch of the future union's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They also said the dollar remained well-supported vis-a-vis the yen against the backdrop of lingering doubts about the effectiveness of Japan's latest economic stimulus package. \par \par \uc2  Talking to reporters after the speech, Rubin predicted the U.S. economy would likely continue to grow at a solid rate with little pressure on consumer prices. \par \par \uc2  "I think we are on a pretty good track," he said. "The most likely scenario by far is solid growth and low inflation with \par \par \uc2   ups and downs ... as long as we continue to do the things we do \par \par \uc2   and maintain our fiscal discipline." \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4t06d07\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
