\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Late-AM: Dlr Lower; World Bk Seen Selling Earlier \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 1998\par 05:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The U.S. dollar is a touch lower against the Japanese yen in late-morning trading on Tuesday in Singapore, compared with levels seen around an hour ago in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Traders maintain, however, that the slight dip is due merely to position adjustment ahead of the region's lunch break. The dollar's underlying tone remains bid, they say. \par \par \uc2  In earlier trading, both the dollar and the mark fell steeply against the yen on what one trader at a European bank in Singapore said was the sale of $1 billion by the World Bank. \par \par \uc2  'We had them on the 'phone, offering a yard of dollars,' he said, using market jargon for $1 billion. \par \par \uc2  Other traders scoffed at the notion that the supranational body was responsible for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall, with the senior trader at one Japanese bank in Singapore insisting that the dollar sales were executed by Japanese life insurance companies. \par \par \uc2  'Every time the dollar tries the downside, someone blames the World Bank,' he said, adding, 'but the important thing was that everyone understood that this was not the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  With little fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, traders and investors took the opportunity to buy up U.S. dollars at cheaper rates, driving the dollar higher again. \par \par \uc2  At 0335 GMT (11:35 p.m. Monday EDT) the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is quoted at Y131.96, down from Y132.08 at 0200 GMT, but above its earlier low of Y131.65. Late Monday in New York the dollar was at Y132.07. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, the mark is at Y73.81, compared with Y73.84 earlier in Tokyo and Y73.86 in New York late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 28-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0348GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4s03jbc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
