\par\par \b \uc2  Yen cedes ground, BoJ remarks stoke bearishness. \b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 27 (Reuters) - The yen retreated against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, setting four-month lows against the mark, as remarks by a Bank of Japan official fanned speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not yet worried by its fall. \par \par \uc2  Kazuo Ueda, a member of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy-making board, said on Monday a further depreciation of five to 10 percent in the yen's value against the dollar would not pose a very large economic risk to Japan. \par \par \uc2  He also said that he would like to see a cut in Japan's official discount rate, which is already at a record low of 0.5 percent, if economic conditions worsened. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan's tolerance level on dollar/yen is likely to be around 134 or 135 and it looks like the market is going to test its resolve," said Mark Geddes, treasury economist at ABN Amro in London. \par \par \uc2  The yen weakened as far as 73.93 per mark, its worst showing since December 15, 1997, and slid to 132.80 per dollar in the wake of Ueda's remarks. It was also undermined by a drop of 2.26 percent in Japan's Nikkei stock index. \par \par \uc2  By 0745 GMT, the dollar was at 132.62/72 yen from 130.95/05 at the close of European trading on Friday. The mark was at 73.88/93 yen from 72.90/95 late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  While Ueda's comments fanned pessimism about the yen's prospects, they were not enough to overshadow completely the fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. Such wariness was kept alive by Japanese Finance Ministry official Eisuke Sakakibara. \par \par \uc2  He said on Monday that bullish sentiment for the dollar was starting to change and that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was looking for the right time to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  "with the wind" to boost the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The MoF is trying to talk the yen stronger but there is no secret level they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at and their policy is only to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they are going to be successful," said Gerard Lyons, chief economist at DKB International in London. \par \par \uc2  The key to successful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lies in dispelling gloom about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic outlook, which has persisted despite the adoption of an economic stimulus package worth 16 trillion yen, details of which were announced on Friday, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Data out overnight did little to lift such pessimism about Japanese domestic demand, however, with trade statistics for the first 10 days of April showing Japan's surplus soared 113.8 percent from a year earlier, with imports slumping 13.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  DKB's Lyons is therefore looking for further yen weakness. He expects mark/yen to head toward 75, with 133.50 a realistic target for dollar/yen this week. \par \par \uc2  The mark's gains against the yen hobbled dollar/mark, which drew limited support from weekend state elections in Germany's Saxony-Anhalt in which the extreme right profited from a slump in the popularity of Chancellor Helmut Kohl's Christian Democrats. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 1.7958/63 marks at 0819 GMT from 1.7916/21 late in Europe on Friday. \par \par \uc2  There were few market-moving reports on the agenda for the European session, with U.S. March existing home sales at 1400 GMT the only economic report scheduled for release until Japan's March retail sales and industrial production data at 2350 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Some direction may, however, come from the two-day meeting of the Organisation for Economic Co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Development beginning Monday, where Japan's economic revival plans are expected to top the agenda. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese Foreign Affairs Ministry official said on Sunday Japan hoped the OECD would revise up its 1998 Japanese gross domestic product forecast from a 0.3 percent decline in light of Japan's economic stimulus package. ((Swaha Pattanaik, London newsroom, +44 171 542 6284, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4r06rz7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
