\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Dlr Down On MOF Remarks Ahead Of Sakakibara \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 1998\par 04:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by senior officials at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has left the dollar lower against the yen at midday Thursday from levels earlier, with the market anticipating more comments on the way. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs, told reporters earlier that an economic stimulus plan, details of which are to be released Friday, will reflect Japan's will to boost the economy. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but colleague Haruhiko Kuroda said the yen is still too weak. Kuroda, who heads the finance ministry's international finance bureau, also reitereated the ministry's warning that investors should beware of the strong yen risk. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar had gotten as high as around Y130.50, before Sakakibara's and Kuroda's comments, but came off afterward,' said Minoru Shioiri, assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nippon Credit Bank. 'But it bounced off of Y130.00 and looks as though it will stay in the Y130.20-30 range for now.' \par \par \uc2  The dollar is stuck in a narrow range because Sakakibara is scheduled to participate in a panel discussion on the dollar-yen relationship in the context of the Asia economic crisis beginning around 0700 GMT (3:00 a.m. EDT). Since his comments Wednesday that Japanese sales of U.S. Treasury bills 'could occur at any time,' helped spark a dollar sell-off, market players are wary of holding long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  'It wasn't just his comments, it also is the accumulation of long dollar positions being liquidated,' Shioiri said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0215 GMT, the dollar is at Y130.20, down from Y130.40 around 0030 GMT and below Y130.43 in New York late Wednesday. It was at Y131.15 in Tokyo late Wednesday. The dollar is also trading at DEM1.7955, barely up from DEM1.7951 earlier in Tokyo and above DM1.7935 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at DM1.7820 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 23-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0224GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4n03ech\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
