\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar firms on Sakakibara  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  comments. \b0\par\par\uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 23 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar rose against the yen on Thursday after a key Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official cooled speculation over Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vice finance minister for International Affairs told a symposium that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not conduct defensive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain a certain \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  level. \par \par \uc2  "He's saying they don't want to defend one number," said Francis Breedon, senior foreidgn exchange strategist at Lehman Brothers in London. \par \par \uc2  At 0855 GMT, dollar/yen had recovered to 130.49/59 yen from an earlier low of 129.91, but still down from Wednesday's late European trading level around 130.80/90. Dollar/mark was trading at 1.7919/24 compared with 1.7932/37. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the reaction to Sakakibara's comments underlined the market's sensitivity to any talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only one day before the Japanese government is set to announce details of its latest economic stimulus package. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively and pushed dollar/yen down sharply on April 9 and 10 after the market failed to react to earlier details of this economic package. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen bulls were restrained by further comments from Sakakibara, who said Japan's economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate were at a significant turning point. He said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only when it believes the yen will rise. \par \par \uc2  "He's saying 'don't believe we won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 '," Lehman's Breedon said. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said they expect the package and any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only be a temporary stop on dollar/yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  "We believe that probably after this package is out of the way, dollar/yen will move higher," said Jane Foley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara's comments come on the heels of comments from Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami, who said Japan's economy continues to be stagnant with strong downward pressure overall, but he expected the economic stimulus plan to have good effects in terms of an economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  In other European action, dollar/mark was softer on the lingering expectations Germany's Bundesbank may raise interest rates ahead of the European Union summit at the start of May. \par \par \uc2  "There is the expectation the Bundesbank may announce rate rise ahead of the May meeting," said Foley. But she expected the Bundesbank would hold off to the latter half of the year. \par \par \uc2  Foley said she expected the Bundesbank would try to squeeze every ounce of growth out of its economy ahead of the start of monetary union before it raises rates to narrow the interest rate gap between itself and higher yielding EMU hopefuls. \par \par \uc2  "The more convergence there is on (economic) growth, the more it will be easier to seek convergence on interest rates," she said. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc was a bit softer, but held steady off recent lows on safe-haven buying before a vote that could prompt the dissolution of the Communist-dominated state Duma lower chamber in Russia. \par \par \uc2  Communist leader Gennady Zyuganov said the party's ruling body had decided to advise a wider leadership meeting on Thursday to stick to its opposition to Sergei Kiriyenko, President Boris Yeltsin's candidate for prime minister. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc firmed to 1.4821/31 francs per dollar from 1.4854/64 in late European trading on Wednesday, and firmed against the mark to 82.75/78 from 82.82/85. \par \par \uc2  ((Paul Casciato, London newsroom +44 171 542 8968, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4n06tej\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
