\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar/yen ends U.S. down,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  fears cap. \b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, April 22 (Reuters) - The dollar ended lower against the yen after influential Japanese official Eisuke Sakakibara indicated Japan could cash in some of its vast U.S. investments to support its beleagured \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Still pressuring dollar/yen was an overnight remark from Sakakibara, vice finance minister for international affairs, that Japan stood ready "anytime" to convert U.S. Treasury bonds into dollars to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The Treasury (bond) comments were very much out of character," said Ben Strauss, a vice president at Bank Julius Baer and Co. \par \par \uc2  "It could be that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is around the corner again," he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 130.35/40 yen down from 130.55/65 at the open and Tuesday's 131.25/35 close. Dollar/mark ended at 1.7944/49, inside and essentially flat versus the opening quote of 1.7940/50. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara's comment at a Tokyo symposium seemed to reflect irritation that the yen remained weak after two big rounds of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before Easter and a statement by Group of Seven finance officials the following week, welcoming Japanese steps to boost its economy and strengthen the yen. \par \par \uc2  After Japan's recent market action, talk was widespread that Japan had sold about $12 billion in Treasury securities to raise the cash. \par \par \uc2  Due to its huge trade surpluses, Japan has amassed the world's largest war chest of dollar reserves, estimated at more the $200 billion. It is the largest foreign holder of U.S. government bonds, with some 25 percent of Washington's debt. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday Japan is expected to detail the 16 trillion yen package of measures to revive its faltering economy. Investors fear that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may time \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the announcement, as it has done on with previous economic packages. \par \par \uc2  A cabinet vote on the Japanese plan may come Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark bounced from a near three-month low at 1.7820 after several German central bankers threw cold water on speculation that German interest rates would soon rise. But the recovery was capped by talk of European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offers in the 1.7950 region, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was lifted after Bundesbank council members Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher, Reimut Jochimsen and Johann Wilhelm Gaddum all said there was no reason to increase German interest rates now. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of people are talking about a rate increase by the Bundesbank before EMU starts to set things to the right tone for the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Diane Hirschberg, a director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank of Montreal. "But there's been lots of comments that they're not going to raise rates." \par \par \uc2  The mark strenghtened on Monday and Tuesday on expectations that German interest rates would soon rise, converging with the rest of Europe before monetary union on January 1. \par \par \uc2  Also quashing such speculation late Tuesday, Italy trimmed a key lending rate, showing yields elsewhere in Europe could decline toward Germany's, rather than the other way round. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the pound slipped to $1.6709/19 from $1.6722/32. The dollar eased to 1.4857/67 Swiss francs from 1.4865/75 and to Canadian $1.4315/20 from C$1.4318/23. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar fell to $0.6518/23 from $0.6525/30. \par \par \uc2  ((-Alden Bentley, 212 859 1667)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4m07011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
