\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar firms on dimming German rate rise prospects. \b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 22 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar strengthened to above 1.79 marks on Wednesday after two Bundesbank council members dampened recent speculation of a rise in German rates. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher said in an interview with German radio station InfoRadio on Wednesday that he saw no need to raise German interest rates. Kuehbacher also said the Bundesbank had no interest in allowing the dollar to slide against the mark. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank vice-president Johann Wilhelm Gaddum told German daily newspaper Boersen-Zeitung in an interview that he saw no acute need to act on German interest rates now. \par \par \uc2  At 0740 GMT dollar/mark was trading at 1.7927/37 marks from lows around 1.7815 marks in Asian trading and Tuesday's late European levels around 1.7862/72. Dollar/yen slipped to 130.75/85 yen from Tuesday's 131.22/32. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the Bundesbank is becoming concerned about rising market speculation that it will raise interest rates on the back of strengthening economic growth statistics. \par \par \uc2  "They are suggesting that there is no need to raise interest rates at this stage and therefore there is no need for dollar/mark to go lower," said Keith Edmonds, chief analyst at IBJ International in London. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said market speculators believe the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to raise interest rates ahead of launch for European economic and monetary union (EMU) for domestic reasons. \par \par \uc2  A rise in German rates would also narrow the interest rate gap with higher yielding countries such as Italy, Spain and Ireland. \par \par \uc2  "The market is at the upper limit of what is conceivable for rates by the end of the year and the Bundesbank is telling us that," said Kit Juckes, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Natwest Markets. \par \par \uc2  Contracts for three-month Euromarks traded around 3.70 percent, indicating a 50 basis points rise in interest rates between now and December, Juckes said. \par \par \uc2  "They (the Bundesbank) don't want the market to dictate to them the pace of monetary policy," Juckes said. \par \par \uc2  Late on Tuesday, the Bank of Italy announced a 50 basis point cut in its discount rate to a 26-year low of 5.0 percent, and cut its Lombard rate to 6.5 percent from 7.0. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen slipped in morning trade after Eisuke Sakakibara, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, warned investors of the risks of a higher yen and said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had ample reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The latter remark raised speculation of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  coinciding with the latest economic stimulus details due on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "There are worries about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and we are coming into a holiday period where the Bank of Japan can take advantage of thinner markets," said Edmonds. \par \par \uc2  Japan will announce full details of its latest 16 trillion yen economic stimulus package on Friday. The last big package announcement was followed by aggressive Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to knock back the dollar. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Golden Week holidays begin on April 29. \par \par \uc2  ((Paul Casciato, London newsroom +44 171 542 8968 fax +44 171 542 5293, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4m06yqq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
