\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar/mark down on rate concern in morning Europe. \b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 21 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar opened European trading broadly weaker, but under heavy pressure against the mark on expectations of a rise in German interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Economists said dollar/mark slid under mounting pressure from speculation the Bundesbank is likely to raise short-term German interest rates long before the Federal Reserve contemplates interest rate rises in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  "The Fed is on hold for a long-time and you are going to have to set that against short-term expectations for a rise in German rates from the Bundesbank," said David Brown, chief economist at Bear Stearns. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said increasing speculation of a rise in German rates was likely to find support in stronger-than-expected German M3 growth and expectations for a rise in the March Ifo business index, prompting some long dollar/mark liquidation. \par \par \uc2  "The market is getting geared up for a possible rate hike, plus it is long dollars," said a dealer at a major U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank reported German March M3 rose an annualised 5.1 percent compared with expectations for a 3.1 percent rise. \par \par \uc2  At 0835 GMT dollar/mark was trading at 1.7888/93 marks from 1.8022/27 in late European trading on Monday. Dollar/yen was also down at 131.51/61 from Monday's 132.27/37. \par \par \uc2  West German Ifo business climate index was unchanged at 98.8 in March just below expectations, while the East German Ifo rose to 107.6 from 106.3 February. \par \par \uc2  Economists also said that while the German data may support prospects of a German recovery, Bundesbank rate decisions must begin to take into account the fast-growing economies of its soon-to-be partners in Europe's economic and monetary union. \par \par \uc2  "The worry for the Bundesbank is not what's going on in its own backyard, but the overheating out there in EMU land," said Bear Stearns' Brown. "The Bundesbank will be acting as a pan-European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Traders also said liquidation of long sterling/mark positions weighed on dollar/mark as sterling/mark slipped to 3.0045/55 from Monday's 3.0258/63. \par \par \uc2  Concerns the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might seek to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on dollar/yen coincident with details on Friday of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest economic stimulus package and debate over further fiscal reform also cast the dollar down. \par \par \uc2  Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs Eisuke Sakakibara said on Tuesday that excessive yen weakness is undesirable. Sakakibara is scheduled to give a speech on Wednesday and appear at a discussion on the dollar Thursday. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, former prime minister Noboru Takeshita argued against revisions to the fiscal reform law, being considered by current Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto. \par \par \uc2  The law requires the government to halve the budget deficit to within three percent of gross domestic product and eliminate deficit-financing bonds by fiscal 2003/04. \par \par \uc2  But financial market participants are concerned that if the government does not extend that target date, it will be unable to make income tax cuts promised by Hashimoto, permanent. \par \par \uc2  Hashimoto is to announce his decision on what changes will be made to the fiscal reform law at a meeting on Wednesday of his Fiscal Structural Reform Council, of which Takeshita is a member. \par \par \uc2  ((Paul Casciato, London newsroom +44 171 542 8968 fax +44 171 542 5293, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limit