\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/mark ends U.S. lower amid sterling/mark slump. \b0\par\par\uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, April 20 (Reuters) - Dollar/mark closed lower, indirectly pressured as the pound tumbled against the German unit and traders took profits on sterling longs before key UK economic data later in the week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was little changed, supported by a firm mark/yen but capped by ongoing fears of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There is still interest in buying mark/yen. That in itself was contributing to relative softness in dollar/mark," said Robert Lynch, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Paribas Corp. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was steady against the dollar, after falling overnight. Its slide below 3.02 marks came as investors bet that the spread between British and German interest rates would narrow in favor of the mark, eroding support for the pound. \par \par \uc2  Cable closed at $1.6755/65, up from $1.6750/60 at the open. Dollar/mark was at 1.8007/12, down from 1.8075/85 and dollar/yen ended at 132.10/20 compared to 132.20/30. \par \par \uc2  The mark has recently been garnering strength from speculation that German money market interest rates, near 3.3 percent, must move higher to converge with other European rates before monetary union in January. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Bank of England policymaker Charles Goodhart told a British newspaper over the weekend that there were signs of a slowdown in the UK economy. \par \par \uc2  The bank's monetary policy committee has been split over the direction of interest rates in recent months and weak data could tilt them in favor of easing the key 7.25 percent bank rate, which would make pound investments less attractive. \par \par \uc2  Sterling hit a 8-1/2 year high near 3.11 marks in late March as traders bet the British \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to ratchet up key interest rates in order to prevent rapid economic growth from igniting inflation. \par \par \uc2  "There are a lot of profits to be taken in sterling-mark - it's huge," said Diego Giurleo, a treasury vice president at Royal Bank of Canada. "A lot of people think the ride is over for now, they're getting out. \par \par \uc2  Britain reported its public sector borrowing requirement was 7.2 billion pounds in March, bringing the full-year deficit to 922 million pounds, the lowest since 1990/91. \par \par \uc2  The pound was little moved on the PSBR but traders will pay closer attention to Thurdsay's March retail sales figures, after a British industry group said earlier this month that retail sales were the poorest since September 1995. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, preliminary data on first quarter British gross domestic product will be scrutinized for signs that the economy has come off the boil. \par \par \uc2  dollar also rose against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite fears that Japan could enter the market to support its beleagured unit, as it did before Easter. \par \par \uc2  Early on Monday, key MOF official Haruhiko Kuroda, said he was strongly concerned about the yen's fall and that Japan would take decisive action on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said the specter of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to hang over the market at least until Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party details its 16 trillion yen economic stimulus package. Japan faces intense international pressure to boost domestic demand instead of exporting its way out of recession. \par \par \uc2  Spotlighting the effects of the weak yen overnight was Japan's custom's-cleared trade surplus, which jumped 57 percent in March from a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the dollar slipped to 1.4970/80 Swiss francs from 1.4985/95 and to Canadian $1.4279/84 from C$1.4296/01. The Australian dollar stood at $0.6463/68, up from $0.6459/64. \par \par \uc2  ((-Alden Bentley, 212 859 1667)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4k072xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
