\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar up but off its highs vs yen by late Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0611 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     132.00/05\tab \tab 132.50-131.84\par  USD/DEM     1.8073/78\tab \tab 1.8120-1.8066\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, April 20 (Reuters) - The dollar was up but well off \par \par \uc2  its earlier highs against the yen by late Tokyo on Monday, \par \par \uc2  capped by lingering speculation of possible dollar-sales \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was also cautious about selling the \par \par \uc2  yen too aggressively before the Japanese government unveils \par \par \uc2  details of its economic package later this week. \par \par \uc2  "People are cautious about surprises being included in the package. Also, the market is wary that the BOJ might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars soon after the package announcement," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past have coincided with the government's economic policy announcements, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ conducted aggressive dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on April 9 and 10, after the government of Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto announced on April 9 the outline of a 16 trillion yen economic stimulus package. The government is expected to unveil final details of the package around Friday. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar briefly rose as high as 132.50 yen after stop-loss buy orders were triggered around 132.10-20 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's earlier gains were driven by speculators who bought the greenback and quickly sold it take profits, a senior dealer at a Japanese city bank said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's trade data for March had limited impact on the dollar/yen, as it was within market expectations, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's March trade surplus jumped 56.5 percent from a year earlier to 1.25 trillion yen. A Reuters poll of economists had produced an average forecast of a 53 percent rise in the surplus to 1.22 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  The contentious trade surplus with the United States rose 19 percent compared with a year earlier to 449.24 billion yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar briefly slipped back below 132 yen by mid-morning on profit-taking, but it quickly moved back above that level on buying related to setting up of fresh investment trust funds, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There was also talk of stop-loss buy orders around 132.50/60 yen and option-linked dollar offers slightly below that level. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said they doubted that rumoured stops were big enough to push the dollar above 133 yen in the near term. \par \par \uc2  "The market is jittery about BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Comments by Mr Kuroda were effective in reminding the market of that risk," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, director-general of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's International Finance Bureau, told reporters on Monday he was strongly concerned about the fall in the yen. \par \par \uc2  He said that given Japan's March trade data announced earlier, a fall in the yen was not desirable because it would make a decline in the trade surplus difficult to achieve, even if Japan's economy recovered. "We will take decisive action on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  as needed," Kuroda said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was slightly down against the mark, following mark buying against the yen by U.S. fund operators. \par \par \uc2  The mark stood at 73.13/16 yen as of 0643 GMT, compared with 72.86 yen in New York on late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Some U.S. fund operators were also setting up dollar short positions versus the mark to hedge against risks of seeing a sharp correction in New York stocks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 131.75/85 yen and 1.8088/93 marks in New York on Friday. ((Kanta Watanabe/Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4k070sy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
