\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Kuroda -2: Asked Whether U.S., Japan Views Different \b0\par\par\uc2 143 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1998\par 02:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Nikkei/Dow Jones)--The head of the international finance bureau of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. can discuss coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at any time. \par \par \uc2  Asked by a reporter inside the ministry whether he thought there was a difference between U.S. and Japanese views concerning coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Haruhiko Kuroda said: 'No, there isn't. The U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  can discuss concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time.' \par \par \uc2  Kuroda also said that the market should understand the communique released by the Group of Seven nations at the end of their meeting in Washington Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'If investors understand the communique, they should be able to figure out the position of the G-7 countries,' Kuroda said. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0025GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4h037jz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
