\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr eases vs yen in early Tokyo on profit-taking. \b0\par\par\uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, April 17 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0010 GMT -- \par \par \uc2      *Dollar down against yen in early Tokyo on profit-taking \par \par \uc2  ahead of weekend amid lingering speculation of possible \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      *Dollar at 131.33/38 yen and 1.8031/41 marks, versus \par \par \uc2  131.70/80 and 1.8040/50 marks in late New York on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      *But dollar bids by Japanese institutional investors and \par \par \uc2  dollar demand related to setting up of fresh investment trust \par \par \uc2  funds seen limiting dollar's downside. Japanese importer bids \par \par \uc2  also detected below 131 yen. \par \par \uc2  *Some Japanese exporters also interested in buying back dollars below 131 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers said dollar remained on uptrend against yen after Group of Seven (G7) nations failed to reverse market's bearish outlook for yen in their meeting on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  *But market still wary about possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week. \par \par \uc2  *"The latest remarks from (senior MOF official Eisuke) Sakakibara had a very stern tone. So the market is cautious about BOJ action," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  *Sakakibara, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, said in Washington he has "grave concerns" about recent exchange rate moves and was unhappy with current dollar/yen level. \par \par \uc2  *Talk of stop-loss dollar buy orders at 132.20, 132.30, and 132.50 yen. But dealers said short-term players are likely to try to lock in profits before weekend if dollar rises to near 132 yen. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar moved narrowly against mark in early Tokyo. Dealers said they expected mark to retain firm tone but dollar's decisive fall below 1.80 marks unlikely in Tokyo trade. \par \par \uc2  2300 GMT - *Dollar edged down against yen in early Asia, slightly under pressure after comments by Eisuke Sakakibara. \par \par \uc2  *Profit-taking emerged ahead of weekend, but Japanese investor bids likely to limit dollar downside. *"I don't think Sakakibara's remarks will have lasting impact today. I don't think other G7 members are that unhappy about current dollar/yen," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  *Indeed, other G7 officials, including Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami, said earlier on Thursday in Washington they were not concerned about latest dollar rise versus yen. \par \par \uc2  *Asked about substantial dollar rise after G7 meeting, Hayami said: "I'm not concerned about it and I don't think the movement was a major one." \par \par \uc2  *French Finance Minister Dominique Strauss-Kahn also said on Thursday he was not concerned about dollar/yen levels. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4h079h8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
