\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ April 10 Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Put At $18 Bln - Nikkei \b0\par\par\uc2 165 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 1998\par 20:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Nikkei)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to prop up the value of yen may have been even bigger than originally believed, The Nikkei Financial Daily reports in its Friday edition. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo money-market insiders now estimate that on April 10 in Tokyo, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold roughly $18 billion to purchase Y2.35 trillion. Earlier estimates had put the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at anywhere from $5 billion to $15 billion. \par \par \uc2  As evidence in support of the higher figure, the insiders point to April 14, the day BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions executed the previous Friday were settled. \par \par \uc2  The Tokyo money markets had expected that fiscal receipts April 14 would absorb Y600 billion from the system. But the actual drainage of liquidity swelled to Y2.95 trillion. \par \par \uc2  The theory holds that the gap between the two figures reflects the actual size of the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-04-98 \par \par \uc2  1822GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4g0373m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
