\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE-Yen late trade calm, wary of cenbanks. \b0\par\par\uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 16 (Reuters) - The yen ended European trade on a relatively calm note on Thursday but the market remained wary as it balanced the bias toward a weaker yen against the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yen declined as expectations of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased after Wednesday's Group of Seven (G7) meeting. But caution remained over possible solo action by the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/yen strength may back down a bit, but the market will still tread warily tomorrow on continued fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Claudio Piron, treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  The yen fell almost two percent against the dollar from its pre-G7 levels on Wednesday to test a one-week low against the dollar of 132.05 in European trade. By 1500 GMT it recovered some poise and stood at 131.78/88 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The G7 fell short of endorsing joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  action but were in agreement in avoiding excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls and they would continue to cooperate in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when needed. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of people feared we would have a strongly worded statement," said Teis Knuthsen, chief economist at SE Banken. "Instead, we got more pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  for tax cuts and no support for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So the knee jerk reaction is correct." \par \par \uc2  The G7 praised Japan's efforts to stimulate its domestic economy which would help correct the excessive weakness of the yen. But they also urged Japan to implement quickly a strong programme of fiscal measures and structural reforms. \par \par \uc2  "What the G7 are saying to Japan is 'you provide some more aggressive fiscal measures and we'll provide the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mark Geddes, treasury economist at ABN-Amro in London. \par \par \uc2  Until then, dealers remained wary of another spell of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep yen bearishness in check. \par \par \uc2  "But this is only likely to slow the inevitable depreciation of the yen," said one U.S. bank dealer in London. \par \par \uc2  Market focus was looking towards Friday's U.S. trade data and a Bundesbank council meeting. \par \par \uc2  Analysts played down the recent speculation of a German interest rate hike, mindful that the German economy does not yet warrant higher rates. Monetary policy decisions from Germany are also unlikely to take place until after Europe's economic and monetary union starting line-up is decided in early May. \par \par \uc2  U.S. trade data, meantime, has been garnering more attention recently with the market growing more wary of the country's expanding current account deficit. A widening gap tomorrow could see dollar gains erode, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  "If we see a worse than expected trade deficit we will see an initial decline in the dollar, but that's normal. With substantial growth in the US, and because of the Asian crisis, you can expect to see deterioration in the deficit, so the trend will not come as a surprise," said SE Banken's Knuthsen. \par \par \uc2  An average of analysts' forecasts point to a $11.8 billion shortfall in the U.S. February trade balance compared with a 12.0 billion deficit previously. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, sterling extended its earlier gains after comments from UK Chancellor Gordon Brown saying the current strength of the pound would not prompt short-term decisions. \par \par \uc2  Sterling shrugged off an early slump after a gloomy British Chambers of Commerce economic survey which said, among other things, UK exports were at seven-year lows. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the relative yield attraction of holding sterling as well as lingering expectations UK interest rates are yet to peak was still keeping the pound in demand. \par \par \uc2  Sterling/mark stood at 3.0561/68 in late Europe, down from a session top of 3.0625 marks but well above late Wednesday's 3.0295/305 marks. Cable was firm at $1.6912/22 from $1.6838/45. \par \par \uc2  ((Andrew Reierson, London newsroom +44 171 542 6745, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4g07cxx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
