\par\par \b \uc2  Yen's weak trend seen unaltered after G7-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kanta Watanabe \par \uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 1998\par 09:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 16 (Reuters) - An agreement by the Group of Seven (G7) industrialised nations to avoid excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation is unlikely to change the weak trend of the yen, dealers and analysts in Tokyo said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But the market was cautious about selling the yen too aggressively, due to speculation the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In a communique issued after their meeting on Wednesday, G7 members said it was important to avoid excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation which could exacerbate large external imbalances. \par \par \uc2  They added that they supported steps taken by Japan aimed at stimulating domestic demand, reducing external imbalances and correcting the yen's excessive depreciation. \par \par \uc2  "The communique itself was not out of the ordinary. Its contents were in line with expectations and contained no surprises," said Ryohei Muramatsu, manager of treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Commerzbank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The dollar briefly rose more than one yen in post-G7 trading in Tokyo on Thursday, as fears of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by G7 nations receded following comments by U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Rubin said in a news conference after the meeting that the G7 session had not included discussion of possible joint action in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prop up the yen. He also reiterated his support for a strong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Kenneth Landon, director and senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell in Tokyo, said Rubin helped to relieve the market's worries about possible coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Rubin specifically said he still supports a strong dollar and on top of that there was no discussion about coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That was really the key to the whole meeting," Landon said. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, said after the meeting that the G7 communique indicated coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the comments from Rubin and Sakakibara seemed to suggest possible discord between Japan and the United States over \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, although Rubin said he shared Japan's concerns over the weak yen. \par \par \uc2  "The conflicting comments from U.S. and Japanese officials gave an impression the two countries are not acting in harmony," said Takuma Kurosawa, chief manager of the international treasury division at Mitsubishi Trust and Banking Corp. \par \par \uc2  "So the dollar drew bids after the meeting on the view that the possibility of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was small." \par \par \uc2  But dealers said they were cautious about buying dollars too actively in the short term, as the BOJ could still act alone to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  "If the yen continues to weaken substantially, the BOJ is highly likely to step in, alone if it has to, to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. So the market is cautious about chasing up the dollar," said Kurosawa of Mitsubishi Trust. \par \par \uc2  Deutsche Morgan Grenfell's Landon said: "The communique specifically mentions 'excessive depreciation of the yen'. This phrase may be used by Japanese authorities to scare the market in the future." \par \par \uc2  Aggressive dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ last week sent the dollar tumbling more than six yen, or 4.5 percent, in just two trading days. Some dealers estimated the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have amounted to well over $10 billion. \par \par \uc2  But Deutsche Morgan's Landon said the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could only help to slow the dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  By \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BOJ would only be taking the role of a "public-service provider of cheap dollars", Landon said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was around 131.32 yen in late afternoon trade in Tokyo, up from 129.93/03 yen in New York late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4g07cmy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
