\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market sees no threat of joint yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Astrid Zweynert \par \uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 1998\par 12:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 16 (Reuters) - Joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yen remains a distant prospect after G7 finance ministers failed to produce a common strategy to help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Group of Seven communiqui issued on Wednesday was in line with previous statements, emphasising G7 agreement to monitor exchange rate moves and cooperate as appropriate. The statement also stressed the need to avoid excessive declines which could cause large external imbalances. \par \par \uc2  But unlike previous statements, the Washington communiqui singled out Japan and the yen by saying the G7 supported appropriate steps by Japan to stimulate domestic demand-led growth, which would also help to correct excessive depreciation of the yen. \par \par \uc2  "It's quite clear that the G7 is not going to act," said Cameron Crise, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at SBC Warburg in London. "Japan has to sort out its economy, and until it does so, joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be effective. \par \par \uc2  "It's unusual they actually mentioned Japan but it's not surprising given the state of its economy." \par \par \uc2  Inconsistent comments after the meeting by U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin and top Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Eisuke Sakakibara suggested there is no unanimous agreement on joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this stage. \par \par \uc2  Rubin said the G7 did not discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while Sakakibara said the statement implied possible joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that he was extremely satisfied with outcome of meeting. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, Rubin had reiterated his support for a strong dollar but also said he shared Japan's concern about the weak yen. \par \par \uc2  The threat of solo Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  loomed over the market though and is likely to rein in yen bears if losses accelerate again towards the 6-1/2 year low of 135.42 yen set in early April. \par \par \uc2  "The G7 left it to the BOJ to do whatever it can to prevent sharp yen losses," said Kirit Shah, chief strategist at Sanwa International in London. \par \par \uc2  "Unless the market is convinced that Japan is doing enough to boost its economy it will take the full firing power of the BOJ to spark a yen rally to 128 or 127 yen." \par \par \uc2  The BOJ engineered a yen rise of over 4.5 percent - or six yen - last week when it took the market by surprise with dollar sales of as much as an estimated $10 billion ahead of the Easter weekend. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen fell to a low of 127.35 but recovered after the G7 meeting, trading around 131.33/43 at 0900 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "While the G7 talked about excessive weakness in the yen, it seems they are content to leave the onus on the Japanese to correct this by stimulating their economy," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economist Europe at Bank America in London. \par \par \uc2  A weak yen helps Japan's exports, thus fuelling speculation that recent bouts of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are merely a brake on excessive yen weakness rather than an effort to reverse the trend. \par \par \uc2  Joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only likely to be effective once \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has set the economic recovery train into full motion with structural reform as well as further fiscal stimulus. \par \par \uc2  Analysts argue it would be ineffective to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the massive weight of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market of the 1990s is simply too big to bully, with a daily turnover of over $1.2 trillion. \par \par \uc2  The G7 nations' appetite for joint action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has waned since its heyday in the 1980s when \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was backed up by major policy moves such as the 1985 Plaza Agreement and the 1987 Louvre Accord. \par \par \uc2  Rubin, who worked for U.S. investment bank Goldman Sachs for over 25 years, knows this all too well, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Timing is everything on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The BOJ succeeded in pushing the yen higher when it combined \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with an announcement of policy initiatives. \par \par \uc2  It did so last December when it sold dollars for yen for the first time since 1992 in the wake of a surprise announcement of tax cuts and again last week, when \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was twinned with news of further tax cuts. \par \par \uc2  But the "law of diminishing returns" on repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has allowed the dollar to turn the screws again on the yen - and the trend is likely to continue, analysts said. ((London newsroom, +44 171 542 7792, fax +44 542 52 93, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4g07cjo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
