\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar gains against yen as Tokyo is urged to reform. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 1998\par 23:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, April 16 (Reuters) - The dollar rose against the Japanese yen on Thursday as concerns over Tokyo's sluggish economy mounted after the world's leading industrialized nations offered no new help to pull Japan out of crisis. \par \par \uc2  One day after the Group of Seven's finance ministers and central bankers urged Japan to boost its economy, U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin warned Tokyo must generate new growth as Asia could not recover with Japan's economic health in doubt. \par \par \uc2  Traders, newly confident the United States and its partners would not join forces with Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the dollar lower through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , again sold yen for dollars overnight. \par \par \uc2  "The G7 nations said there is a possibility they could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the reality is that they are not going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the dollar is going higher," Chris Melendez, senior dealer as Sanwa Bank California, said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended trading at 131.80 yen, nearly two yen above Wednesday's 130 yen closing rate, with dealers saying gains might be limited now as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fresh from heavy dollar sales last week, could still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Economic Planning Agency Minister Koji Omi said the government would announce its package of economic stimulus measures before the end of the month, dealers remained skeptical about the yen's prospects. \par \par \uc2  "We should see the dollar trading between 125 and 135 yen until we see some independent strength from the Japanese economy," Mike Malpede, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Refco Group Ltd., said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar gained slightly against the German mark as analysts said Wednesday's talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be planning to raise interest rates was premature. \par \par \uc2  Considering Germany's 12.1 percent unemployment rate and low inflation rates, analysts said the Bundesbank would likely delay any interest rates hikes, needed to help European rates converge in time for Europe's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  union, until later in the year. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 1.8045 marks, up from 1.8015 marks on Wednesday and jumped to 1.5033 Swiss francs from 1.4965 Swiss francs. \par \par \uc2  The dollar however slipped against the British pound as the unit climbed to $1.6915 from $1.6855. It also slipped against the Canadian dollar to C$1.4334 from C$1.4377. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4g075qy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
