\par\par \b \uc2  Japan/MOF Kuroda -2: Speaking To Reporters \b0\par\par\uc2 138 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 1998\par 05:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--A top official at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday that coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is always a possibility. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to a group of reporters, Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the international finance bureau, said: 'The U.S. and Japan share the same view on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.' \par \par \uc2  He also said excessive yen weakness is 'undesirable', and that the statement put out in Washington on Wednesday by finance ministers and central bankers from Group of Seven (G-7) leading industrialized nations is clear. \par \par \uc2  'The market will understand the G-7 statement,' Kuroda said. \par \par \uc2  He declined to comment on unconfirmed rumors that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the yen earlier Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0328GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4g0362r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
