\par\par \b \uc2  G-7/Rubin -2: Remarks Before Start Of Matsunaga Meeting \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 1998\par 17:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said Wednesday he would discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates during a morning meeting with Japan Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury secretary, who was speaking at a photo opportunity before heading into a private meeting with Matsunaga, was asked if there was linkage between joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's implementation of demand-led measures to stimulate its economy. \par \par \uc2  'No. We'll be discussing Japan's economy and the importance of reestablishing domestic demand-led growth in Japan. Totally independent of that would be what ever discussion takes place about exchange rates,' Rubin said. \par \par \uc2  'Were going to have a discussion of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I don't know what the discussion will be, we haven't had it yet,' he said. \par \par \uc2  There has been widespread speculation in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may come to some accommodation over at least joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster the yen. This speculation followed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which included the Federal Reserve Bank of New York executing dollar sales on behalf of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 1