\par\par \b \uc2  Japan/Politicians/Rate Hike -4: Yen Won't Prompt Rate Hike \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 1998\par 11:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  First Boston's Okada said that although \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen, it isn't likely to raise interest rates merely on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . 'The BOJ could raise interest rates later, when the economy has strengthened somewhat,' he said. \par \par \uc2  'A gradual depreciation against the dollar is acceptable,' said Yamakawa, though he sees a worrying possibility of competitive devaluations, particularly by China, if the yen slides to around Y150 against the dollar from Y130 at present. \par \par \uc2  Last week, in a dramatic loosening of fiscal policy, Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto announced a Y16 trillion economic stimulus package. Duke said a tighter monetary policy, combined with a looser fiscal policy, might be viable at some point, but only after the financial system has become more stable. \par \par \uc2  BOJ governor Hayami has repeatedly made similar comments, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will retain current monetary policy for now and that ultra-low interest rates are still having economic benefits. \par \par \uc2  Although Nonaka and other senior LDP officials are influential, they have no formal control over policy, which is up to Hayami and a new policy board established this month under a new law designed to make the BOJ more independent of political pressure. \par \par \uc2  Economists see the statements by Nonaka and others as politically motivated rhetoric. Politicians can gain stature within the LDP by pronouncing on economic policy, and with elections to the upper house of Parliament looming in July, they are anxious to appeal to voters. \par \par \uc2  The LDP receives much of its support from rural areas that tend to have concentrations of elderly citizens. As the intricacies of monetary policy are beyond most voters, a call for a rate hike amounts to a call for the government to send more money to poorer rural areas, a political tradition with a long history. \par \par \uc2  'It's politicians' talk,' said Salomon's Young. \par \par \uc2  -By Nathan Lewis; (813) 5255-2929; nlewis@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0901GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4f034x0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
