\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Seen Generous Wed: Demand High, Accumulation Period Ends \b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 1998\par 01:43\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan is likely to take a\par generous stance at its usual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  time of 0020 GMT on\par Wednesday (8:20 p.m. EDT Tuesday), traders said.\par    Wednesday is the last day of the current reserves\par accumulation period, and reserves should end even with the\par requirement, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to be generous\par at the regular \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  time to keep money market rates\par stable, they said.\par    "The market was a little tight late Tuesday, and I don't\par think the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can afford to be neutral," said a\par money market trader.\par    The bank may leave reserves about Y200 billion or Y300\par billion above the requirement, the same as Tuesday, and drain\par excess funds later outside the market, he said.\par    The key unsecured rate for overnight call money will\par likely be around 0.47%, the same as Tuesday, traders said.\par Tuesday's weighted average was 0.48%.\par    The money market saw a shortage of yen funds late\par Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Many Japanese banks sold yen to the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par two sessions ago when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to support the yen against the\par dollar.\par    Because the transactions settled Tuesday, some market\par participants were having trouble securing yen funding in the\par money market, traders said.\par    -By Karen Hawkins; 813-5255-2939; khawkins@ap.org\par    Michiyo Seki; 813-5255-2941; mseki@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  04-14-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1943EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du4e00zul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
