\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Up On Cautious Domestic Bids; BOJ Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 1998\par 02:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar is edging higher in early Tokyo trading Tuesday compared with its levels late in New York Monday, as the absence of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  since its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week prompted cautious buying by Japanese trust banks and pension funds. \par \par \uc2  Although there are lingering concerns that the BOJ will again enter the market before or after the Washington meeting of finance ministers and central bankers of the Group of Seven (G-7) nations Wednesday, traders expect the dollar to mostly hover in the Y129 territory for the rest of Asian trade unless the BOJ steps in. \par \par \uc2  Even if the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar won't fall much below Y127.50 and will likely start picking up shortly afterwards, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'There are still fears the BOJ may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , solely or jointly, but that's not going to stop investors from bidding the dollar,' said a trader at a Japanese bank. 'There's just too much demand for the dollar.' \par \par \uc2  Others said the BOJ isn't likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the dollar breaks above Y130, and said the return of all of the major markets Tuesday for the first time since the Easter holidays began will lessen the impact of any action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'A lot of people are coming back to the market, and will add a lot of liquidity, so the BOJ can't remain as dominant a player,' said Yasuhisa Morikuni, vice president of financial markets at Bank of America in Tokyo. 'The reason the BOJ was so successful on Friday was because of the lack of liquidity.' \par \par \uc2  Around 0030 GMT (7:30 p.m. EST), the dollar is trading at Y129.70, up from Y129.47 around 0001 GMT and above Y129.56 in New York late Monday. The dollar was quoted at Y129.00 late in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DEM1.8239, lower than DEM1.8242 earlier but above DEM1.8238 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at 1.8243 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 14-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0041GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4e032pi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
