\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr slips below 130 in Europe after MOF comments. \b0\par\par\uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 14 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar dropped from 130 yen after a Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said excessive weakness in the yen was not favourable. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar slipped back from levels above 130 yen on the comments, ahead of a meeting of G7 finance ministers and central bankers in Washington this week and after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which knocked dollar/yen down to as low as 127.35 yen from above 133 yen late last week. \par \par \uc2  But economists said a steady U.S. economy and disappointment over the details of Japan's latest fiscal package will keep dollar pressure on the yen in spite of the BOJ's presence. \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT the dollar was trading at 129.77/87 from 130.18/23 in late European trading on Thursday and Monday's late North American levels at 129.64/69. \par \par \uc2  "The market wasn't really happy with the package and the BOJ took the opportunity to blast the dollar down, but the yen's going to be under dollar pressure until the market sees concrete fiscal policies put in place," said Sandy Batten, senior economist at Citibank in London. \par \par \uc2  He said the pressure from the dollar would be partly restrained in the short-term by fears of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the Group of seven (G7) nations meeting this week. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, head of the International Finance Bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , warned the market against pushing up dollar/yen ahead of the meetings on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  He told Reuters that "excessive weakness of the yen is not favourable" and that G7 nations will discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at a meeting in Washington this week. He added that he believed other G7 nations felt the same way about the yen. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said it was unlikely the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the G7 will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the market this week given that most dealers are back after the Easter holidays on Friday and Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The market will be frightened of it this week, but there is no reason to be," said Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns in London. "The dollar is like a boxer with his nose bloodied, he'll probably stagger around for a while, but then he'll fight back." \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark slipped back a little on Tuesday in sympathy with dollar/yen's restraint, edging down to 1.8178/83 marks by 0840 GMT from 1.8207/17 in late European trading on Thursday and 1.8235/40 in late North American trading on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the economic picture in the United States is likely to continue buoying the dollar. \par \par \uc2  They said the U.S. Federal Reserve was unlikely to opt for a change in interest rates, in spite of powerful demand in the U.S. economy, until the impact of the Asian crisis is known. \par \par \uc2  "The underlying U.S. economy is probably stronger than the Fed would like it to be, but the Fed is unwilling to act until they can fully gauge the impact of the Asian crisis." The U.S. will report inflation on Tuesday when it releases its March consumer price index at 1230 GMT. Market economists expect a month-on-month rise of 0.1 percent compared with a rise of 0.1 percent in February. U.S. March retail sales, also due at 1230 GMT, are expected to rise 0.1 percent compared with 0.5 percent in February. \par \par \uc2  ((Paul Casciato, London newsroom +44 171 542 8968 fax +44 171 542 5293, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4e07hvp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
