\par\par \b \uc2  Yen Cross - Yen selling resumes by Tokyo midday. \b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 14 (Reuters) - Yen selling had resumed in Tokyo cross trade by midday on Tuesday, backed by firm demand from Japanese investors for fresh investment in overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said aggressive dollar-selling/yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) last week did not alter the fact that prospects for the Japanese economy remained weak. \par \par \uc2  "It's a simple question - Why should the yen be bought when (Japanese) stocks and bonds are reflecting the weakness of the economy?" said a dealer at a Japanese commercial bank. \par \par \uc2  The mark was quoted at 71.46/49 yen at 0310 GMT, up from around 71.10 yen in late New York on Monday. \par \par \uc2  A senior dealer at a city bank said a mark rise to 71.50 yen was possible after its rise to 71 yen overnight. \par \par \uc2  Other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted healthy gains against the yen, dealers said. Sterling was at 217.03/15 yen against around 216.29 yen in late New York on Monday, while Swiss franc was at 86.29/34 yen, against around 85.84 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Last week's heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ made investors hit the sidelines for a while. But they are now worried about missing a chance to invest overseas," said a senior dealer at a Japanese long-term credit bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said yen selling may accelerate if no statement suggesting strong concerns about a weak yen is issued at the Group of Seven (G7) meeting on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Finance ministers and central bankers of the G7 industrialised nations are expected to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the meeting. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that despite verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday morning by Haruhiko Kuroda, head of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's International Finance Bureau, the yen's downtrend remained intact. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was lifted up to 130.25/35 yen by 0316 GMT, against Monday's New York closing of 129.64/69 yen. \par \par \uc2  As a result of heavy BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York on Thursday and in Tokyo on Friday, the dollar hit a recent low of 127.40 yen on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the recent movements in the yen, MOF's Kuroda told Reuters: "Excessive weakness of the yen is not favourable." \par \par \uc2  He said G7 nations would discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at the Washington meeting. He added that he believed other G7 nations felt the same way about the yen. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8570 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4e07ecd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
