\par\par \b \uc2  = \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Keeps Yen At Forefront For April 15 G-7 \b0\par\par\uc2  By Uta Harnischfeger \par \uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 1998\par 18:39\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    FRANKFURT (Dow Jones)--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par behalf of the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the yen late last\par week gives the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  automatic top-billing at\par the Group of Seven Industrialized Nations' meeting in\par Washington on April 15, analysts and officials say.\par    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last Thursday and Friday, carried out in\par part by the Federal Reserve Of New York, highlighted the\par dilemma facing policy-makers: On one hand a weak yen will\par bolster Japan's feeble economy, but on the other, it's a\par time bomb for U.S.-Japanese trade relations, with the\par potential to heighten existing trade tensions between the\par two countries.\par    Many market watchers expect world monetary officials to\par place growing trade imbalances in second place to the\par international community's wish to prop up Japan's economy.\par    Accordingly they expect relatively soft language on\par dollar-yen levels to emerge from the meetings in Washington\par this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Most don't expect anything but verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par emerge from the meeting of G-7 finance ministers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governors. They say the G-7 feels that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economy\par isn't quite ripe to support coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  yet.\par    "Coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is still off the table at\par Wednesday's G-7 meeting," said David Gilmore, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par analyst at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Analytics in New York.\par    "(U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert) Rubin's strong dollar\par credentials are intact, and Thursday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't\par mark a shift U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy," added Gilmore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  04-13-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1239EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1192 4211 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du4d00y76\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
