\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Curr Acct Surplus/Asia -2: Yen Seen Weakening Further \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 1998\par 04:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Exports to Asia comprise about 35% to 40% of Japan's total exports, Shipley said. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said the current account surplus isn't likely to continue rising sharply in the medium to long term. Economists agreed. \par \par \uc2  'Although they've been saying this for some time, this time they have got it right for once,' said Matthew Poggi, an economist at Lehman Brothers Japan Inc. 'Exports to Asia will continue down. And while exports to the U.S. remain strong, they may slow as the U.S. economy slows, something we see happening in the fall.' \par \par \uc2  The ministry official also said a series of economic stimulus steps taken by the government since last year should soon boost domestic demand, increasing imports and helping to curb the current account surplus. However, analysts were more skeptical of this. \par \par \uc2  'They'd like it to be true, but it's not.' Poggi said. 'Imports are going to continue to slow quite a bit.' \par \par \uc2  With exports and imports falling, the economy is showing further signs of a recession, which is going to put even more pressure on the yen, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently hit a six-and-a-half-year low of Y135.42 against the dollar before verbal and actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japanese authorities sent the dollar back below Y130.00. But the weakness of the economy means the Bank of Japan remains unable to raise the official discount rate from its historic low of 0.50%, leaving it with few options to keep the yen from weakening further, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  'The implications for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are for it to fall to around Y140.00,' said Schroders' Shipley, who believes the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen last week will eventually prove futile. \par \par \uc2  'They're playing with fire,' Shipley said of reports that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent between $5 billion and $7 billion protecting the yen. 'They can't do that all the time. Foreign reserves can disappear very quickly.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 13-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0231GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4d033g7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
