\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Dlr Up Vs Yen As U.S. Funds Short-Cover \b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 1998\par 04:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--U.S. funds and Japanese institutional investors bought the dollar against the yen to cover short positions, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher at midday in Tokyo Monday compared with its levels early in the session. \par \par \uc2  They were lured by perceptions the dollar is a bargain at the intraday low level around Y127.70, and because the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the morning by selling dollars for yen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'U.S. funds, who were expecting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and were short on dollars, bought them back against the yen,' said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  However, they added many expect the Bank of Japan to step into the market if the dollar rises above Y129.50, which is capping the dollar above Y129.00. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar was weighed down by data showing Japan's current account surplus rose sharply again in February, as well as comments over the weekend from a senior ruling Liberal Democratic Party official on the need to raise interest rates, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Thay said if the dollar were to break below last week's low of Y127.50, a run spurred by stop-loss dollar selling could take the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as low as Y125.00. \par \par \uc2  Japan's current account surplus for February, before adjustment for seasonal factors, rose 97.1% from the year-earlier month to Y1.665 trillion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The LDP's deputy secretary-general, Hiromu Nonaka, said: 'Now that the direction of the economic stimulus package has been set, I believe conditions have been created for the BOJ to review the discount rate, and I hope it will do so.' \par \par \uc2  Around 0200 GMT (9:00 p.m. EST), the dollar is trading at Y128.55, up from Y128.18 round 0100 GMT (7:30 p.m. EST) but below Y128.94 in New York late Friday. The dollar was quoted at Y128.03 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DM1.8238, higher than DM1.8230 earlier in Tokyo and unchanged from DM1.8238 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at DM1.8168 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 13-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0221GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4d033g0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
