\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dollar Down Vs Yen On Foreign Fund Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 1998\par 03:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The specter of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is giving foreign players a reason to unwind long-dollar positions first and ask questions later in Tokyo Monday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  As a result of that selling, led by U.S. funds, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is lower in early Tokyo trading compared with its levels late in New York Friday. \par \par \uc2  The stronger yen also has pushed the Deutsche mark up aginst the dollar compared with its levels in New York. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Bank of Japan is quite likely to step into the market if the dollar rises above Y129.50. Conversely, they said if the dollar were to break below last week's low of Y127.50, a run spurred by stop-loss dollar selling could take the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as low as Y125.00. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said that the market will push the dollar higher if the BOJ stays out. \par \par \uc2  'If the BOJ doesn't show its presence this week, the dollar will go back up Y5 very quickly to Y133.00,' said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar was also weighed down by data showing Japan's current account surplus rose sharply again in February. Japan's current account surplus for February before adjustment for seasonal factors rose 97.1% from the year-earlier month to Y1.665 trillion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Remarks over the weekend by a senior ruling Liberal Democratic Party official on the need to raise interest rates also gave the yen a lift Monday. \par \par \uc2  Hiromu Nonaka, the LDP's deputy secretary-general, said in a speech in Osaka that the BOJ should begin considering a hike in the official discount rate. \par \par \uc2  'Now that the direction of the economic stimulus package has been set, I believe conditions have been created for the BOJ to review the discount rate, and I hope it will do so,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Around 1000 GMT (9:00 p.m. EST), the dollar was trading at Y128.18, slightly up from Y128.15 around 0001 GMT (8:01 p.m. EST) but below Y128.94 in New York late Friday. The dollar was quoted at Y128.03 late in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also trading at DM1.8230, higher than DM1.8215 earlier but below DM1.8238 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at DM1.8168 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 13-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0108GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4d033cw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
