\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dlr Higher But Capped By BOJ Fears \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kenneth McCallum \par \uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 1998\par 07:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar ended slightly higher in Asian trading Monday compared with Friday's levels, after swinging sharply lower in the morning on selling by overseas funds and Japanese banks wary of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar dropped to an intraday low of Y127.70 at 0021 GMT (8:21 p.m. Sunday EDT) as players began the session by unwinding dollar positions. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plummeted nearly Y4 Friday as BOJ conducted massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout the day to defend the yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yen was also purchased against the dollar Monday on data showing Japan posted an unexpectedly large current account surplus in February, as well as on weekend remarks by Hiromu Nonaka, the deputy secretary-general of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party, who said the BOJ should begin considering a rise in the discount rate. \par \par \uc2  But dollar buying by Japanese institutional investors supported the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at its lows against the yen, pushing it up to around Y129.00 late in the Tokyo session. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they remain nervous about the possibility of further BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly Monday because the BOJ could take advantage of extremely thin holiday conditions to drive the dollar down. \par \par \uc2  'The market is afraid of any unexpected moves that may shake' the dollar against the yen, said Yasuhisa Morikuki, assistant vice president at Bank of America in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said it's widely believed the BOJ would enter the market if the dollar again approaches Y130.00, because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen wanting the yen to be at a reasonable level ahead of the Washington meeting of finance ministers and central bankers of the Group of Seven (G-7) nations Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0530 GMT (1:30 a.m. EDT), the dollar is quoted at Y129.00, above Y128.94 Friday in midday New York. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at DM1.8243, higher than DM1.8238 Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 13-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0536GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4d031bv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
