\par\par \b \uc2  Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Expected To Highlight G-7 Meeting This Week \b0\par\par\uc2  By Uta Harnischfeger, Staff Reporter \par \uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 1998\par 21:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones Online News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week on behalf of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen will give the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  automatic top-billing at the Group of Seven Industrialized Nations' meeting in Washington Wednesday, analysts and officials say. \par \par \uc2  Even so, they expect relatively soft language on dollar-yen levels to emerge from the meeting. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Thursday and Friday, carried out in part by the Federal Reserve of New York, highlighted the dilemma facing policy-makers. On one hand, a weak yen will bolster Japan's feeble economy. But on the other, it's a time bomb for U.S.-Japanese trade relations, with the potential to heighten existing trade tensions between the two countries. \par \par \uc2  Many market watchers expect world monetary officials to place growing trade imbalances in second place behind the international community's wish to prop up \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy. \par \par \uc2  Most don't expect anything but verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to emerge from the meeting of G-7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors. They say the G-7 feels that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy isn't quite ripe to support coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet. \par \par \uc2  "Coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still off the table at Wednesday's G-7 meeting," said David Gilmore, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in New York. "(U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert) Rubin's strong dollar credentials are intact, and Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't mark a shift in U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy." \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has brought trade issues to the forefront. \par \par \uc2  "I'm sure (President Clinton) gets daily calls from Chrysler and the likes, and the U.S. is getting increasingly worried about trade issues," Gilmore said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a replay of previous Japanese maneuvering. When Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto announced his first fiscal package in December - which the G-7 heavily criticized at its subsequent meeting in February - the Japanese responded by selling dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  This time, it seems as if Hashimoto may be trying to head off another reprimand from his G-7 counterparts. \par \par \uc2  Last Thursday, the Japanese political leader outlined his long-awaited 16-trillion-yen (about $124 billion) stimulus package. The program includes 10 trillion yen of actual spending, public works projects and income tax cuts. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were disappointed, economists said. Instead of propping up the yen, the stimulus package prompted the yen to plummet in a knee-jerk reaction. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  later that day helped it recover. Following the weekend break, it traded at 129.35 yen to the dollar in late afternoon Monday dealings in Asia, compared with 128.94 yen Friday midday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Now, market watchers say that all Japan can hope for is to win the international community's support for its package. \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1998 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2  1192 4211 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020329du4d00ng8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
