\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo -2: BOJ Action Unlikely Unless Dlr Up Sharply \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1998\par 03:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The dollar will likely find initial resisitence between Y131.50-Y131.70, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Many traders said it is unlikely the BOJ will step in to support the yen Friday unless the dollar gathers significant upward momentum. \par \par \uc2  'If the dollar doesn't accelerate upward, I don't think the BOJ will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Yesterday, I think the BOJ knew that market players would sell the yen on the economic steps (Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto outlined in a speech Thursday), and wanted to stop the yen from weakening too much ahead of the G-7 meeting,' said a senior dealer at a Japanese trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, the U.S is unlikely to jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'I don't think Japan's economic package is enough to move the U.S. to cooperate with Japan in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets,' Bank of America's Morikuni said. \par \par \uc2  Hashimoto said Thursday that his government plans to implement tax cuts exceeding Y4 trillion. \par \par \uc2  But with Japan's economy floundering, there is little reason to buy the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Underscoring this sentiment, Japan's Economic Planning Agency slightly downgraded its assessment of the economy Friday by adding the words 'increasingly severe' to describe the stagnant economy. The economy is stagnant due to weak household spending, falling corporate earnings and flagging capital investment, and has showed signs of increasing severity recently, the EPA said. \par \par \uc2  'It just confirms what we already know,' said a dealer at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  Finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs from the Group-of-Seven industrialized countries are scheduled to meet next week in Washington. \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at Y71.83, down from Y71.90 earlier and below Y71.95 in New York late Thursday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Thursday at Y72.52. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6690, down from $1.6695 earlier and below $1.6707 in New York late Thursday. Sterling was at $1.6688 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Arran Scott 813-5255-2984; amscott@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0115GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4a031rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
