\par\par \b \uc2  Sakakibara -2: After Tax Cut Announcement, BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1998\par 02:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong yen policy is unchanged, a top official at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, vice finance minister for international affairs, said that Japan has 'done what is necessary' for its economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and will continue to 'take necessary steps' in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  His comments followed the announcement Thursday evening by Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto of Y4 trillion in additional tax cuts and the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets overnight in New York. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara said that Hashimoto's measures will 'eventually work to boost Japan's economy,' and that he expects the yen to rise again against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar briefly dropped over four yen overnight in New York to Y129.54 from its intraday high of Y133.59 after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through the Federal Reserve Bank of New York. \par \par \uc2  At 0036 GMT (8:36 p.m. EDT Thursday), the dollar was quoted around Y131.18. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0042GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4a031qb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\