\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  three times on Thursday-BOJ quoted. \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 10 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market three times on Thursday, buying yen for dollars, an Economic Planning Agency (EPA) official quoted BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami as saying on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Hayami was quoted as saying that the BOJ consulted the U.S. Federal Reserve soon after Thursday's announcement of fresh fiscal steps by Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto. \par \par \uc2  "We talked with the Fed and conducted a considerable amount of yen buying/dollar selling, a total of three times," the official quoted Hayami as saying. \par \par \uc2  Hayami was also quoted as saying that following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the dollar had fallen to around 129.50 yen from around 133.50 but that it had moved back up to around 130 yen by late Thursday trade in New York. He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would closely monitor movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during Tokyo hours on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Economic Planning Agency Minister Koji Omi said Japan will aim to achieve real growth in gross domestic product of 1.9 percent in the fiscal year that began on April 1, given economic measures such as four trillion yen in income tax cuts announced on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the government's announced plans so far, including the tax cuts, would be enough to ensure economic recovery, Omi said: "We would like to achieve at least 1.9 percent GDP growth in fiscal 1998/99." \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the announced steps would be enough to ensure 1.9 percent growth, Omi said it was difficult to say as the details of the package had yet to be fleshed out. \par \par \uc2  He added that the prime minister had asked for an economic package to be drawn up by the week of April 20. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4a07jdw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
