\par\par \b \uc2  MOF's Sakakibara expects yen, Japan stocks to rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 10 (Reuters) - Japan's top financial diplomat, Eisuke Sakakibara, said on Friday he expects the yen and Tokyo share prices to rise as a result of government economic policies and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The vice finance minister for international affairs told reporters that Japan "has done whatever is necessary" on the economic and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fronts and that its "strong yen policy is unchanged". \par \par \uc2  Asked as he entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  whether the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight dollar-selling, yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reversed the yen's recent decline, Sakakibara said: "I think the yen will strengthen." \par \par \uc2  Asked if Japanese authorities are ready to move again to support the yen, he said: "Our strong yen policy is unchanged." \par \par \uc2  Asked if Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto's announcement on Thursday of economic measures, including four trillion yen in tax cuts over the next two years, along with the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had turned around weak sentiment on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock market, he said: "They will eventually turn it around." \par \par \uc2  Asked how he expects the Japanese moves to be evaluated at a meeting next week of Group of Seven finance and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs, he said with a laugh: "Ask them!" \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara then noted that U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin had issued a statement overnight in which he welcomed Japan's moves. \par \par \uc2  Rubin specifically welcomed Hashimoto's stimulus announcement and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  interevention, said the U.S. shares Japan's concerns over the yen's fall, and urged Japan to "move quickly to put in place a strong programme" for the economy. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara, asked what case Japan will make at the G7 for its policies, he said: "We have done whatever is necessary, I think." \par \par \uc2  But when pressed whether Japan was ready to do more, Sakakibara only laughed and entered his office. ((Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4a07jds\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
