\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr steady in Tokyo but capped on fears over BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, April 10 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0015 GMT --*Dollar held above 131 yen in early Tokyo, but \par \par \uc2  topside capped on caution over BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it \par \par \uc2  stepped in to sell dollars overnight in New York. \par \par \uc2      *Japanese Vice Finance Minister Eisuke Sakakibara said \par \par \uc2  Friday morning he expects yen to strengthen and Japan's "strong \par \par \uc2  yen" policy is unchanged. Separately, senior Finance Ministry \par \par \uc2  official Haruhiko Kuroda said yen's weakness still excessive. \par \par \uc2      *Interbank trading dominated activity, with buying on dips \par \par \uc2  demand pushing up dollar to around 131.50 yen in early trade, \par \par \uc2  but further gains were limited. \par \par \uc2  *Activity thin as overseas operators on Easter holidays, which exaggerated fluctuation of dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers said dollar expected to find support around 130.50 yen on possible bids by importers and bargain hunters. \par \par \uc2  *"The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight was effective to cap the dollar. At least in the near term, the dollar should be weighed down on sharp rallies, but there are enough buyers waiting to buy dollars on dips," a Japanese commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  *Finance Ministry's Kuroda said on Friday that yen remains too weak despite overnight yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by BOJ, but he predicted yen will rise. \par \par \uc2  *Sakakibara said Japan has done what is necessary on economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and he expected sentiment on yen and Japanese stocks to improve. \par \par \uc2  *Comments by Japanese officials also capped dollar, but unable to drive it down sharply against yen. \par \par \uc2  *With many overseas players away for holidays, Tokyo operators unlikely to build new positions aggressively. Operators could take wait-and-see stance and refrain from active trading, which may keep dollar in range of 130.50 yen to around 131.50/60 yen in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar little changed against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  2302 GMT \par \par \uc2  *Dollar drifted slightly lower in early Tokyo as market turned cautious about bidding it up aggressively following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York overnight. \par \par \uc2  *"The dollar/yen has turned very heavy on the upside after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a city bank dealer said. "With many overseas operators away for Easter, the dollar is unlikely to be volatile here today. Although the market is very cautious." \par \par \uc2  *Activity extremely thin in early trade with light position adjustment sales weighing on dollar. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar's topside expected to be capped around 131.50/60 yen, while investor bids to give support at 130.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  *After overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin saying that the United States shares Japan's concern about recent yen weakness, market expected to be cautious about buying dollars against yen aggressively. \par \par \uc2  *\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman confirmed on Thursday that BOJ bought yen and sold dollars at 1320 GMT on Thursday at around 133.00-133.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  *\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  detected largely through electronic broker systems via New York Federal Reserve Bank. \par \par \uc2  *Japanese Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga said on Thursday that Tokyo took "decisive action" in order to stem yen's weakness against dollar. \par \par \uc2  *Rubin welcomed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster yen but made no mention whether U.S. was joining the action. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar fell as low as around 129.50 yen in overseas markets overnight, but active short-covering protected it on downside, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar shot up against yen in late Tokyo on Thursday after active short-covering emerged as contents of Japan's economic package were not bold enough to satisfy market. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4a07j0r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
