\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Seems Braced For More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  On Dlr-Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kenneth McCallum and Takeshi Takeuchi \par \uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1998\par 10:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed braced Friday for an extended confrontation with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to boost the value of the yen against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent a clear signal that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't want the dollar above 130 yen, and said similar battles could be fought in coming weeks as the market tests the BOJ's resolve. \par \par \uc2  Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came just a day after the BOJ sold dollars for yen through the U.S. Federal Reserve in New York, suggesting a new aggressiveness by the BOJ in defending the yen. \par \par \uc2  'The BOJ will act intensively until investors are convinced of the risks of the yen strengthening,' said Shuji Takano, senior trader of ABN Amro Bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The dollar plunged about four yen in Tokyo Friday to a low of Y127.42 from a morning high of Y131.40. The size of the move was partly due to the thinness of a pre-Easter market, but traders also applauded the BOJ's skill in keeping the market off-balance for most of the day. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese monetary official told Dow Jones that the sales totaled several billion dollars and were conducted repeatedly at various levels. Traders noted sales at Y130.30, the upper Y129 level, the mid-Y128 level and below Y128.00. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ's resolve to bolster the yen appeared to be strengthened by\par the announcement Thursday of a Y16 trillion government package to\par stimulate the economy, traders said.\par    In the weeks before the package's announcement, hopes for strong\par stimulus helped to support the yen. But although the stimulus package\par was Japan's largest ever, it ultimately disappointed financial markets\par because it didn't include permanent tax cuts or radical changes to the\par government's fiscal stringency program.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 10-04-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0859GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1134 4204 55127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4a032ex\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
